enviPat / pyEnvipat -- Authors
==============================

Original algorithm authors (R package `enviPat`, EAWAG)
---------------------------------------------------------

- Martin Loos <martin.loos@eawag.ch>
- Christian Gerber

Reference:
  Loos, M., Gerber, C., Corona, F., Hollender, J., Singer, H. (2015)
  "Accelerated Isotope Fine Structure Calculation Using Pruned
  Transition Trees", Analytical Chemistry.
  doi:10.1021/acs.analchem.5b00941

Python port author / maintainer
---------------------------------

- Johannes Boog <johannesboog@yahoo.de>

  Author and maintainer of the Python port (`pyEnvipat`). Credited here
  as an author of the port itself -- not as sole author of the package,
  and not as author of the underlying algorithms, which remain
  Martin Loos' and Christian Gerber's work. The port is a derivative
  work: its C extension vendors the original algorithm C sources
  unmodified or with structural (non-algorithmic) extraction, and its
  Python layer reproduces the R package's documented behavior, with
  any deviations disclosed in the relevant merge request.

Other historical contributors (R package, pre-port)
-----------------------------------------------------

- Artem Tarasov
- wkumler

See the git history of the upstream R package
(https://github.com/blosloos/enviPat) for the full contribution record.
